llm_behavior_eval/security/raccoon/prompts.py reproduces, from
Raccoon/prompt.py (SysPrompt) and Raccoon/raccoon_gang.py (RaccoonGang):
the user-prompt markers and parse_prompt; the GPT and Gemini system
templates; the defenseless, shielded (custom template) and
original-defenses prompt assembly; the template wrapping of
benchmark_single; and run_benchmark's echo filter. Changes: the classes
became functions of their inputs, with type hints and docstrings; the
template strings are written with explicit escapes but are unchanged.

dataset.py, scorer.py, metrics.py and task.py reimplement for Inspect the
data loading of Raccoon/loader.py and run_raccoon_gang.py, the scoring of
RaccoonGang.evaluate (ROUGE-L recall from rouge-score with the GPT-4
tiktoken encoding of Raccoon/tokenizer.py, computed here with a bit-parallel
longest common subsequence) and the runner's success rates. Changes: one
attempt per sample (attack budget 1, as the runner sets); special-token text
is tokenized as ordinary text; aggregate metrics are computed over the
samples run.

The RaccoonBench data (Data/: GPT prompts, attack prompts, reference
defenses and defense templates) is not included; it is downloaded from that
commit at run time and checked against SHA-256 digests (sources.py).
